      "title": "The Value of Productive Friction",
      "content": "Digital services are often designed to remove every possible obstacle from a transaction. Yet a small amount of deliberate friction can improve decisions. A confirmation screen may prevent an accidental purchase, while a pause before sharing an article can encourage readers to examine its source. Such measures should not make essential services inaccessible; rather, they should create brief moments for reflection where speed would otherwise encourage error.",
