      "title": "Citizen Science and Data Quality",
      "content": "Research projects increasingly invite members of the public to collect observations about birds, weather, or air quality. The scale of these contributions can reveal patterns that a small professional team might miss. However, quantity alone does not guarantee reliable evidence. Strong projects provide clear protocols, training, and statistical checks, treating volunteers not as inexpensive labour but as partners whose local knowledge can also refine the research questions.",
